  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">SPRiNG - Strengthening Peace and Resiliance in Nigeria</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Strengthening Peace and Resilience in Nigeria (SPRiNG) programme is a four-year programme funded by the UK Foreign and Commonwealth Office (FCDO) and managed by Tetra Tech International Development. It commenced in May 2024. SPRiNG will support a more stable and peaceful Nigeria, the impact of which will be that citizens will benefit from reduced violence and increased resilience to the climate. It will achieve this by supporting Nigerian stakeholders to become able to respond to conflict, security, justice, and natural resource management challenges in target areas. Working with Nigerian stakeholders, SPRING aims to: (a) support locally led enhancements to natural resource management, conflict prevention, violence reduction, security and justice (b) work to remove or lessen the impact of critical barriers to peace; and (c) support partnerships for peace with likeminded international partners to multiply funding spent by FCDO.</narrative>
  </description>
